from Feminist Viewpoint[J].海外英语,2017,(04):144-146+149.\n[171] 肖瑞.A Brief Comparison of the Two Characters-Jane Eyre and Tess[J].海外英语,2013,(14):223-224+236.\n[172] 姜莉霞.简·爱与苔丝的性格及其命运对比分析[J].镇江高专学报,2013,26(04):26-29.\n[173] 林丹.夏洛蒂·勃朗特《简·爱》与托马斯·哈代《德伯家的苔丝》之比较[J].黑龙江教育 学院学报,2010\n[174] 王怡.浅议哈代的自然主义观在《德伯家的苔丝》中的体现[J].赤峰学院学报(汉文哲学社会科学版),2012,33(08):153-154.\n[175] 李素芬.维多利亚时代女性抗争的命运——对简·爱和苔丝的比较与分析[J].名作欣赏,2013,(27):45-46.\n[176] 张轶,许炜.“勃朗特姐妹”笔下的生态女性主义：话语的呈现方式、叙事解读[J].宿州学院学报,2025,40(10):40-46.\n[177] ④ 学位论文（标识：[D]）\n[178] 刘瑶瑶.恩格斯女性解放思想及其当代价值研究[D].山东师范大学,2024.\n[179] 高雪. 19世纪中叶到20世纪初的英国妇女选举权运动[D]. 内蒙古:内蒙古大学,2012. DOI:10.7666/d.y2145864.\n[180] 江潇潇. 论维多利亚小说女性意识的觉醒——以《简爱》为例[D]. 广西:广西师范学院,2012.\n[181] 夏丽莹.《简爱》、《傲慢与偏见》、《红楼梦》中女性人物对比研究[D].哈尔滨理工大学,2013.\n[182] 张凤. 托马斯·哈代的现代女性意识[D]. 山东:山东大学,2008. DOI:10.7666/d.Y1420564. \n[183] 张敏.从女性主义视角解读《德伯家的苔丝》中苔丝的悲剧 [D].四川师范大学, 2013.\n[184] 王佩. 从女性主义的角度分析《简·爱》[D]. 陕西:西北大学,2010. DOI:10.7666/d.y1679373.\n[185] 徐苏. 《德伯家的苔丝》中哈代生态女性意识研究[D]. 四川:西南财经大学,2017.\n[186] 胥彦. 苔丝与简·爱两位女主人公不同命运的比较研究[D]. 黑龙江:东北农业大学,2017. DOI:10.7666/d.Y3231768.\n[187] ⑤ 专利（标识：[P]）\n[188] ⑥ 标准（标识：[S]）\n[189] ⑦ 网络或在线文献（标识：[EB/OL]）\n[190] ⑧ 新闻报纸（标识：[N]）\n[191] ⑨ 研究报告（标识：[R]）\n[192] ⑩ 其他（标识：[Z]）\n[193] 致  谢\n[194] （注：一级标题，加粗，三号黑体字；内容为小四号宋体，1.5倍行距；另起一页）\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775190274915}}
{"type":"message","id":"ec61721e","parentId":"c307425c","timestamp":"2026-04-03T04:25:05.068Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the content of both the paper and the format template. The user wants me to modify their paper to match the format template.\n\nLooking at the format template, it contains:\n1. General requirements (总体要求) - 10 rules about thesis format\n2. Title page information\n3. Abstract requirements (Chinese and English)\n4. Table of contents structure\n5. Section formatting requirements (1, 1.1, 1.1.1 style numbering)\n6. Figure and table formatting\n7. Formula formatting\n8. Conclusion requirements\n9. Reference formatting (different types: M, J, C, A, D, P, S, EB/OL, N, R, Z)\n10. Appendix requirements\n11. Acknowledgment requirements\n\nLooking at the paper content, it seems like the paper is already quite well-formatted. The user probably wants me to go through and ensure it matches all the specific formatting rules in the template.\n\nHowever, since both files are in DOCX format and I need to modify the paper's format, I should:\n1. First understand the exact formatting differences between the template and the paper\n2. Then edit the paper's XML to match the required format\n\nBut this is quite a complex task - essentially reformatting an entire academic thesis. Let me think about what specific changes need to be made.\n\nLooking at the format template rules:\n1. Content should be accurate\n2. Chinese should use standard characters per GB/T15834\n3. Terminology, symbols should be consistent per relevant standards\n4. Number usage per GB/T15835\n5. Units per GB3100, GB/T3101, GB/T3102\n6. Template is based on GB/T7713.1-2025\n7. Title should not exceed 25 characters\n8. Notes should be in footer\n9. Bachelor's thesis uses double-sided printing, page numbers in Roman then Arabic\n\n\n10. A4 paper with specific margins (30mm top, 25mm bottom, 25mm left, 20mm right)\n\nThe template also specifies heading hierarchy with section numbers, figure and table numbering formats, and reference types. For the paper itself, I need to ensure the title page structure aligns with the template's requirements, verify all sections follow the 1, 1.1, 1.1.1 numbering system, and confirm figure and table formatting matches the specified conventions. I should use python-docx to systematically inspect the current formatting and identify what needs adjustment to bring the paper into full compliance with the template specifications. I need to clarify which file is which. The user mentioned the first file is the format and the second is the paper to be modified. Looking at the file names - bb79401b is labeled as the template (格式) while a19e512c contains the actual paper content including the thesis title about 19th century British literature and the student's name 张旭玲. So I should be editing a19e512c to match the formatting requirements specified in bb79401b. Looking at the structure more carefully, the template file contains the complete format specification with all the rules and requirements, while the paper file is essentially the same document - it has the template content plus the actual student thesis title \"19世纪英国文学女性意识的差异化表达—以简•爱与苔丝为例\" and student name 张旭玲 filled in. So I'm working with two instances of essentially the same template document, where one has been partially completed with the student's specific information.\n\nTo actually modify the formatting, I should use python-docx to systematically adjust the paragraph styles, spacing, indentation, font sizes, and other formatting specifications outlined in the template sections.\n\nGiven the complexity of reformatting an entire thesis to match precise template specifications, I think the most practical approach is to discuss with the user which specific formatting changes they want addressed, since there could be many adjustments needed. Alternatively, if they want me to just apply the template formatting directly, I should unpack the template DOCX file, extract its styles and formatting XML, and then apply those same styles to the paper DOCX file. to modify their paper's format to match the template requirements. This means I'll need to systematically compare the formatting rules in the template against what's currently applied in the paper document, then make the necessary adjustments to align them. The key changes would involve font specifications, spacing, indentation, and other typographical standards that are detailed in the template's opening sections.","thinkingSignature":"7138199f9f857d353d3407c9916d52390145f90455f4032e0da2412410c689bf"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0afhliccssry_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"C:\\Users\\zhang\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python313\\python.exe -c \"\nimport zipfile\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nimport codecs\n\ndef get_docx_text(path):\n    ns = {'w': 'http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main'}\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(path, 'r') as z:\n        with z.open('word/document.xml') as f:\n            tree = ET.parse(f)\n    root = tree.getroot()\n    paragraphs = []\n    for p in root.iter('{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main}p'):\n        texts = []\n        for t in p.iter('{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main}t'):\n            if t.text:\n                texts.append(t.text)\n        if texts:\n            paragraphs.append(''.join(texts))\n    return paragraphs\n\n# Read format template\ntemplate_paras = get_docx_text(r'C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\media\\outbound\\bb79401b-62e2-48ca-a586-b7dbb1aa9cc7.docx')\n\n# Write to file with UTF-8\nwith codecs.open(r'C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\workspace\\format_content.txt', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for i, p in enumerate(template_paras):\n        f.write(f'[{i}] {p}\\n')\n\nprint('Done writing format content')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":39200,"output":1258,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":73292,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775190274918,"responseId":"061e7401441d01c58d7eabb044b09a85"}}
