{"type":"message","id":"f3c0fa62","parentId":"f9d123a0","timestamp":"2026-04-03T04:28:26.724Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the script ran successfully. But I see a few issues:\n\n1. The encoding of the paper content is garbled - the text shows as Chinese characters encoded incorrectly. This is because the document is stored in a Chinese encoding, but my analysis code was trying to read UTF-8.\n\n2. Looking at the paragraph analysis - the sample shows the format template content (elements 0-14 seem to be the format template \"总体要求\" etc.), not the actual paper content. That's because the paper file seems to have the same content as the template file. Wait, let me re-check.\n\nActually wait - looking at the file I read, the paper starts with \"附件1.贵阳人文科技学院本科毕业论文（设计）基本模板\" which is the template title. \n\nSo I'm realizing the first 31 items in my paper_content.txt are actually from the template file, not the paper itself. The real paper content begins at item 31 with the actual thesis title \"19世纪英国文学女性意识的差异化表达\". Let me trace through the file structure more carefully - it looks like the paper file might have a different structure than I initially thought, with the template content appearing first before the actual thesis content starts. I see the issue now - the paper_content.txt file only contains the format template information, not the actual formatted paper. The script extracted the template metadata instead of the thesis content itself. Looking at the file listing, item [31] in paper_content.txt shows the thesis title in Chinese, which suggests the actual paper content is there but I need to verify what the script actually extracted versus what should have been extracted.","thinkingSignature":"191690ddec91de7238996a8375ba6e5081c611af42b5a17409a936f302e2a1d1"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_7f4dtcm5iz9q_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"C:\\Users\\zhang\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python313\\python.exe -c \"\nimport zipfile\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nimport codecs\n\ndef get_docx_text(path):\n    ns = {'w': 'http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main'}\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(path, 'r') as z:\n        with z.open('word/document.xml') as f:\n            tree = ET.parse(f)\n    root = tree.getroot()\n    paragraphs = []\n    for p in root.iter('{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main}p'):\n        texts = []\n        for t in p.iter('{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main}t'):\n            if t.text:\n                texts.append(t.text)\n        if texts:\n            paragraphs.append(''.join(texts))\n    return paragraphs\n\n# Read formatted paper\npaper_paras = get_docx_text(r'C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\workspace\\paper_formatted.docx')\nprint(f'Total paragraphs: {len(paper_paras)}')\nprint()\nprint('Last 30 paragraphs:')\nfor i, p in enumerate(paper_paras[-30:]):\n    idx = len(paper_paras) - 30 + i\n    print(f'[{idx}] {p[:80]}')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":54467,"output":646,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":87947,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775190490964,"responseId":"061e74d9cdcef2f56bb4b85dff70fb5b"}}
